From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Measure governor pressure as work past the deadline

A simulation chunk runs until the frame's deadline by design (app.js
runChunk -> staged step(deadline)), so its duration equals the budget the
governor itself set. The governor compared that duration with the same
budget: a full frame read as pressure, YELLOW cut the next budget by 25%,
the shorter chunk read as GREEN, and so on. iPhone diagnostic
DX-1792300927407 (980,000 assets) shows chunks taking 4 ms of a 4 ms live
budget and 9-11 ms of a 7.5-10 ms calendar budget, with 80-253 level
changes per 10 s window.

The YELLOW level now uses the overrun: for a chunk, the time past its
deadline; for create/finish, which are indivisible, their whole duration.
ORANGE/RED (long and hard tasks), the calendar throttle, thresholds and
budget factors are unchanged.

tests/governor-overrun-signal.cjs drives the scheduler with chunks that
stop at their deadline, like the staged transaction. On the previous code
it fails with 1,687 level changes in 30 s of live play; with this change
ordinary work makes no level change and real overruns still raise YELLOW
and ORANGE. Synthetic stages with an injected clock; not an iPhone
benchmark. package.json and source fingerprints are not updated.

